{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/127927-aether-fueled-generator","id":127927,"title":"aether 'fueled' generator","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-07T19:28:54-07:00","id":127927,"title":"aether 'fueled' generator","content":"Has anyone else had stockpiles as generators come up? for instance the bigger and more complicated the more it can store so if a turbine generator like that is found in hydroelectric dams was used as a stockpile it could pose interesting implications. Because these generators would still be operating it would produce electricity.<br /> <br /> now in game that wouldn't be the path I'd take. I'd have a generator designed to run off aether that would act as a stockpile but slowly diminish aether pool like an exploited gadget. Just so I don't feel like I am exploiting an over sight(an understandable one)<br /> <br /> so again has anyone encountered any unique uses of stockpile rules? Either grand plans or simple unique quirky uses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T04:37:57-07:00","id":128143,"title":"","content":"Enslaved Unchained to power up infrastructure with Aether, just saying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T05:13:36-07:00","id":128158,"title":"","content":"Ephsy is that not a scary thought? The way stockpiles preform under aether's influence is no accident but hand written laws drawn up by the God machine. A fate worse than death for captured unchained. Wired directly into the 'heat vents' they serve as slaves once more but now self aware of their lack of freedom.... oh I hope my st doesn't see this.<br /> edit:jumbled a thought at the end","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2909,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","user":"Mr.F.I.X.","date":". 05-08-2014, 08:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T10:40:52-07:00","id":128361,"title":"","content":"I wonder what demons in primitive, tribal societies would use for stockpiling. The idea came up, because via stockpile rules, human technology hasn't been very useful for very long in terms of complexity. Would the demons of, say, the cave man days have had to create not-yet-existing technology for stockpiles, or rely on Infrastructure or God-made technology? Would a cooking fire count (a sort of aether bonfire, ever burning like the burning bush), back then or in very untechnological societies/eras, or even today? I mean, I suppose a simple hand made water/wind wheel wouldn't be horrifically unfeasible for a demonic caveman to build (even if the humans hadn't).. but no way he'd have access to anything capable of storing larger amounts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T11:43:36-07:00","id":128410,"title":"","content":"Tools count as tech in a way but that is a very good question. Would tools like a spear be able to contain aether? Such can be made into gadgets so maybe but obviously with such low complexity maybe only a single point. Then if this become a stockpile how would it affect the tool? Ect","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T14:00:47-07:00","id":128503,"title":"","content":"Undying cell phones, cars that run forever with no gas, infinitely producing generators... Sounds like a feature and not an oversight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thread Reaper <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">\uff1c(\u00b4 \u055e)\u0a0a( \u055e )\uff1e\ufeff</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/377-xanandithras","name":"Xanandithras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar377_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T14:52:56-07:00","id":128534,"title":"","content":"Only reason I mention possible oversight is if you went to the extent of powering a hyro electric turbine type generator for example I would assume on that scale aether could slowly diminish. But then again such an anomaly would draw the God machines attention more likely than not so even if there were no degradation of aether it would have drawback.<br /> <br /> \u200bI am interested in possible unique or interesting uses of stockpiles.<br /> <br /> side note: my idea of potential degradation on that scale is to give a player such as myself a reason to do more than power up and forget. On the scale I am mentioring a 'then forget' as a player would feel hallow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T19:16:39-07:00","id":128691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/127927-aether-fueled-generator?p=128143#post128143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Enslaved Unchained to power up infrastructure with Aether, just saying.</div> </div> </div> </div> Wasn't this the plot of the QuickStart?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thread Reaper <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">\